{
  "schema_version": "0.0.1",
  "id": "snare-punch",
  "name": "Punchy Snare",
  "category": "modular",
  "notes": "snarePunchSeed: the old open hi-hat heard as \"a cool tight, fuzzy snare\",\nrebuilt organic — the classic head (snare's variant, 210 / 315 Hz) plus a\nmodal-plate wire layer with Buzz Hold (round 3: \"still a bit noisy\", TailRattle\n168 -> 0 with the hold). Then retuned for CRACK (2026-09-30, \"sounds fire\"),\nfitted like snareFatSeed: the plate wires move DOWN (centre 7.3 kHz -> 1.2 kHz,\nmodes 1.1-6.1 kHz), the classic head's own 1.8-4.5 kHz wire burst comes back\non at a low level (which makes snare_attack / snare_tail_d live again), and the\nhead drives harder. Crack -26 -> -16 dB, fizz >7 kHz -22 -> -34 dB (at peak 1).",
